BT /F2 15 Tf 72 720 Td (A short glossary) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 691 Td (Chunk. A piece of a document, cut before indexing, that the retriever scores as a whole.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 667 Td (Chunk size. How long each piece may be, counted in characters or in tokens.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 643 Td (Overlap. Text repeated at the start of a chunk from the end of the one before it.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 619 Td (Splitter. The step that decides where one chunk ends and the next begins.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 595 Td (Embedding. A list of numbers that stands for what a chunk means, used to compare it with) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 580 Td (a question.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 556 Td (Index. The store of chunks and their embeddings that a search runs against.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 532 Td (Retriever. The step that scores every chunk against a question and returns the best.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 508 Td (Top k. How many of the best-scoring chunks a search hands on to the next step.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 484 Td (Reranker. A second, slower model that reads the question and each returned chunk) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 469 Td (together.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 445 Td (Hybrid search. A search that combines keyword matches with embedding matches.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 421 Td (Context window. The amount of text a language model can read at once.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 397 Td (Heading path. The headings above a chunk, kept with it so it says where it came from.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 373 Td (Recall. The share of the passages that answer a question that the search brought back.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 349 Td (Precision. The share of what the search brought back that answers the question.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 325 Td (Token. A small unit of text, often part of a word, that models read and count.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 301 Td (Semantic chunking. Cutting where the meaning changes, found by comparing the embeddings) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 286 Td (of neighbouring sentences.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 262 Td (Parent and child. Small chunks searched for precision, each pointing to a larger chunk) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 247 Td (handed to the model for context.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 223 Td (Evidence. The sentence in a document that answers a question, used to check whether a) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 208 Td (search found it.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 72 184 Td (Hit rate. The share of test questions whose evidence came back in the pieces checked.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 40 Td (RAG Playground sample: a primer on chunking) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 510 760 Td (Page 6) Tj ET
endstream
